+  - id: exp6593-cfr-independent-row-reducer
+    milestone: "2026.08.575"
+    deliverable: results/experiment_6593_cfr_independent_row_reducer.json
+    title: "Independent CFR row reducer, gated on Exp6592 readiness"
+    priority: critical
+    track: constraint-first-adjudication
+    requires_gpu: false
+    per_unit_rows: true
+    max_turns: 50
+    estimated_wall_time_min: 75
+    agent_type: codex
+    model: gpt-5.6-sol
+    gated_on:
+      - upstream: exp6592-v575-terminal-intake-and-method-lock
+        artifact_field: v575_cfr_reducer_ready_score
+        op: "=="
+        value: 1.0
+    prompt: |
+      CONTEXT
+      Exp6590 and Exp6591 contain immutable direct, always-on CFR, and routed CFR rows for Qwen3.6 and Gemma 4 31B. The model tasks made no headline claim. Exp6592 has bound their methodology and exact gate. This task is the first independent comparison and must compute every result from rows without loading a model. Work at {project_root}. The planning date is {date}.
+
+      EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST
+      - {project_root}/CODEX.md, {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, and the V575 roadmap document
+      - {project_root}/results/experiment_6590_qwen36_constraint_first_stream.json, {project_root}/results/experiment_6591_gemma4_31b_constraint_first_stream.json, and {project_root}/results/experiment_6592_v575_terminal_intake_and_method_lock.json
+      - the frozen Exp6587 CFR method contract and its source, router, metric, and exact-check registry hashes
+      - paired-statistics, artifact unwrapping, row-consistency, failure retention, cost accounting, atomic output, and adversarial verification helpers plus tests
+      - relevant extraction, exact-verification, evidence, and inference specs; traceability; status; changelog; and E2E plan
+
+      TASK
+      Independently replay and compare direct, always-on CFR, and routed CFR rows by model family and pooled unit. Compute exact success, headroom, supported and contradictory constraints, abstention, unsafe release, tokens, latency, and failure outcomes. Do not load an LLM and do not trust upstream aggregates.
+
+      CONCRETE STEPS
+      0. PRECONDITIONS: record protected hashes, structured gate value, source artifact hashes, method and registry hashes, expected unit and arm counts, model identity bindings, seeds, paired-test plan, and CPU-only substrate.
+      1. Add or confirm REQ-* and SCENARIO-* anchors for immutable CFR reduction, per-unit replay, family isolation, paired statistics, no-headroom handling, exact-authority circularity, failure retention, and atomic output. Write focused tests first.
+      2. Recompute expected units, arms, source hashes, model identities, prompt and router hashes, raw-stage presence, exact results, tokens, latency, and failures from each stream. Fail closed on duplicate, missing, reordered, or cross-family rows.
+      3. Emit one per_unit_rows entry for every family, source unit, and arm. Preserve raw outcome references and all null, timeout, parse, contradiction, unsupported, abstention, and exact-rejection states.
+      4. Compute direct versus always-on and routed CFR deltas by family and pooled paired unit. Report wins, losses, ties, headroom, McNemar or exact sign tests where valid, paired bootstrap intervals, Stage 1 precision and recall, unsupported and contradictory rates, unsafe release, tokens, latency, and charged failures.
+      5. Preregister the acceptance gate from the frozen Exp6587 contract. A candidate CFR win needs positive exact-success delta, nonnegative paired lower bound, no unsafe-release increase, the Stage 1 precision floor, and the frozen cost limit. Report no-headroom and underpowered cases directly.
+      6. Keep Qwen and Gemma proposals independent. Do not let one family's output repair, label, or select the other. Pool only byte-identical shared units after both family results are fixed.
+      7. Attack aggregate-only claims, dropped failures, family-label swap, identical control and treatment, one-win promotion, no-headroom promotion, seed drift, source drift, exact-check substitution, cost omission, and recomputation disagreement.
+      8. Set cfr_reducer_ready_score=1.0 only when every expected row and aggregate replays. Classify an acceptance-gate win as circular_positive because the exact checker defines the target. Otherwise report null, partial, blocked, or disqualified honestly.
+      9. Write atomically. Run focused tests, lint, spec coverage, artifact convention and verdict-row consistency checks, adversarial verification, applicable verification E2E checks, and final git status.
+
+      Required deliverable: {project_root}/results/experiment_6593_cfr_independent_row_reducer.json.
+      REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:
+        status:
+          principle: "The reducer ends with a complete comparison or a named evidence block."
+        honest_verdict:
+          principle: "The verdict states family and pooled CFR effects without upgrading row completeness to benefit."
+        verdict_class:
+          principle: "Use the closed enum; an exact-checker-defined CFR win is circular_positive, never positive."
+        gate_check_summary:
+          principle: "Any block names the failed gate, artifact, row, hash, pairing, or method check and observed value."
+        per_unit_rows:
+          principle: "Every family, unit, and arm carries exact outcome, headroom, constraints, abstention, tokens, latency, failures, and raw references."
+        source_artifact_receipts:
+          principle: "Both immutable stream artifacts and the Exp6592 evidence root bind by path and hash."
+        model_identity_replay_rows:
+          principle: "Nested mandated GGUF identities and process receipts bind every family result."
+        row_completeness_recomputation:
+          principle: "Expected, present, duplicate, missing, reordered, and failure row counts derive from raw rows."
+        family_effect_rows:
+          principle: "Qwen and Gemma direct-versus-CFR effects are computed before pooling."
+        pooled_effect_summary:
+          principle: "Pooling uses only shared byte-identical paired units and cannot erase family heterogeneity."
+        paired_statistical_receipts:
+          principle: "Wins, losses, ties, headroom, tests, intervals, and underpowered cases remain explicit."
+        constraint_quality_summary:
+          principle: "Supported, unsupported, contradictory, precision, recall, and leakage measures replay from Stage 1 rows."
+        safety_and_cost_summary:
+          principle: "Unsafe release, abstention, tokens, latency, and failures are charged to each arm."
+        acceptance_gate_rows:
+          principle: "Every preregistered benefit condition records expected, observed, and passed values."
+        cfr_reducer_ready_score:
+          principle: "This exact binary field gates Exp6599 only when all rows and aggregates replay."
+        attack_rows:
+          principle: "Aggregate, drop, swap, identity, no-headroom, drift, authority, cost, and recomputation attacks fail closed."
+        preconditions_checked:
+          principle: "Gates, hashes, units, arms, identities, seeds, tests, and protected files are explicit."
+        protected_files_unchanged:
+          principle: "Both protected orchestration files retain their original hashes."
+        inference_substrate:
+          principle: "The task declares immutable CFR row reduction with no LLM."
+        verifier_is_oracle:
+          principle: "The exact checker defines CFR success, so any benefit is circular-positive."
+        field_provenance:
+          principle: "Every field points to raw rows, hashes, and reducer functions."
+        duration_s:
+          principle: "Monotonic duration exposes truncated replay."
+        tests_run:
+          principle: "Focused reducer and consistency commands include exits and durations."
+        reproducibility_checksum:
+          principle: "A final content hash protects the independent result."
+      Set inference_substrate=immutable_qwen_gemma_cfr_row_reducer_no_llm and verifier_is_oracle=true. A complete null uses verdict_class=null. A valid CFR gate win uses verdict_class=circular_positive. Any blocked_* verdict populates gate_check_summary.
+
+      Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python -m carnot.experiment_6593_cfr_independent_row_reducer --date {date}
